      "scenario_id": "A",
      "implication_text": "If new evidence supports a sudden failure (for example, the tank outlet failing overnight as the claimant reports), Escape of water cover would move toward established; Gradual leakage exclusion would be re-assessed as not engaged.",
      "next_step": "Collect the outstanding evidence (the plumber, the claimant), then re-run coverage and settlement for the affected issues for human review."
    },
    {
      "scenario_id": "B",
      "implication_text": "If new evidence supports prolonged leakage (for example, staining around the outlet noted by the plumber), Escape of water cover would not be established; Gradual leakage exclusion would become potentially applicable. This needs senior human review.",
      "next_step": "Refer to a senior adjuster with the cited clauses and evidence; no automatic decision."
    },
    {
      "scenario_id": "C",
      "implication_text": "If new evidence is inconclusive, Escape of water cover would remain unresolved; Gradual leakage exclusion would stay open: whether it is engaged could not be concluded.",
      "next_step": "Consider an independent expert inspection."
    }
  ]
}

